<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .inside-iran p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">July 20, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 143 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-07-20</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v48.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL (written LAST by Judge) ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      The July 18-20 cascade — US service member deaths in Jordan, the Kuwait desalination infrastructure strike, and the Darkhovin nuclear plant attack — locks <span class="cite">F2</span> (ceasefire by July 31) at p=0.18 toward likely-NO while compressing <span class="cite">F4</span> (senior talks by Sept 30) to p=0.38 via new Iranian preconditions from the nuclear-infrastructure category; <span class="cite">F3</span> (Brent crude $100 by Aug 3) at p=0.38 is the near-term observable canary, with the Kuwait strike establishing the category of Gulf civilian energy infrastructure attack that closes the remaining price gap if it recurs against Saudi or UAE assets.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">6 active · board rebuilt 2026-07-20 · last reasoned 2026-07-20</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (≤72h)</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F1</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will at least one Iranian ballistic missile or drone physically impact Israeli sovereign territory before EOD 2026-07-23?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 28% (2026-07-20)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-23</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. p=0.28 (Judge concurs with analyst). Iran struck near Aqaba, Jordan July 18 (3 missiles intercepted, 1 in desert). In this resumed phase (since July 7), Iran calibrates strikes against US forces in Jordan, Kuwait, and Iraq — not Israeli soil — to avoid Israeli retaliation opening a second front while the US war is ongoing. During Feb-June war, Iran fired 650+ ballistic missiles at Israel, so operational capability and precedent exist. The July 18-19 geographic expansion into Kuwait civilian infrastructure (desalination plant) is a qualitative step that raises the probability Iran's strike calculus shifts toward Israeli territory. Mojtaba Khamenei's July 18 'unforgettable lessons' statement is addressed to the US, not Israel. 3-day horizon.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if at least one confirmed Iranian ballistic missile, cruise missile, or drone physically strikes and detonates on Israeli sovereign territory (including Israeli-administered Golan Heights) before EOD July 23. Intercepted missiles that do not ground-impact = NO. Missiles landing in Jordanian Aqaba or Syrian territory near Israeli border = NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1 confirmation: Reuters, AP, AFP, or Bloomberg reporting IDF confirmation of physical impact on Israeli territory, OR Israeli government/IDF official statement corroborated by at least one additional TIER1.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If projectiles detonate near the Israel-Jordan or Israel-Syria boundary and territory of impact is disputed = RESOLVE-AMBIGUOUS. If Iran claims a strike on Israel but IDF denies and no physical damage documented = RESOLVE-NO. Interception in Israeli airspace with debris falling on Israeli soil without warhead detonation = RESOLVE-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC official communiqué names 'Zionist entity' as primary retaliatory target</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IDF announces nationwide Home Front Command alert covering all civilian shelters</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Second IRGC ballistic missile salvo targeting Aqaba/Eilat corridor at closer range</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7-30 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F2</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a formal US-Iran agreement explicitly halting active bilateral military exchanges — publicly confirmed by both governments — take effect and hold for ≥72 consecutive hours before EOD 2026-07-31?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">18%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −4pp from 22% (2026-07-20)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-07-31</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Analyst proposed p=0.22; Judge reduces to p=0.18. Iran formally suspended MoU commitments July 18 (Deputy FM Gharibabadi). FM Araghchi: 'No talks on final deal if threats continue.' MFA spokesperson Baghaei: 'We currently have no plans for negotiations.' The US is on its 9th consecutive night of strikes. Qatar-Pakistan mediation channel has gone dormant. A halt by July 31 (Day 24 of this resumed phase) would be faster than any prior ceasefire in this conflict. Judge reduction rationale: casualty-driven political lock-in on both sides (3 US service members killed in Jordan) and the Iran MoU formal suspension create a higher barrier than the 0.22 analyst baseline reflected.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if (a) a US official (White House, State, or CENTCOM) AND an Iranian official (president, FM, IRGC spokesperson, or foreign ministry) both publicly confirm a bilateral agreement to cease offensive military strikes, AND (b) no US airstrike on Iranian territory AND no Iranian missile or drone strike on US forces or Hormuz commercial vessels occurs for 72 consecutive hours before EOD July 31.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1 confirmation of official statements from both sides required.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>A pause in exchanges without a mutual announcement = NO. Technical working-group talks without ceasefire declaration = NO. A ceasefire declared but broken within 72h before EOD July 31 = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar PM or Pakistan PM announces resumed in-person mediation shuttle to Tehran and Washington</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">US observes verified ≥24h pause in airstrikes on Iranian territory</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran FM Araghchi publicly resumes ceasefire language in named statement</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F3</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will ICE Brent crude oil close at or above USD 100.00/barrel on at least one trading day before EOD 2026-08-03?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">38%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp from 38% (2026-07-20)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-03</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. p=0.38 (Judge concurs with analyst). Brent settled ~$84.95 July 15 and closed ~$90.78 July 19 — ~7% gain in four days. $100 requires a further ~10.2% gain from the July 19 close. This requires an additional discrete shock: Iranian attack on Saudi Aramco/ADNOC facilities (~0.12 prob in 14 days), full Iranian naval closure including military-escorted convoys (~0.15), or dramatic escalation to Iranian oil fields. Against: Saudi/UAE remain non-belligerent; US has explicitly avoided Iranian oil fields; EIA reports 8.5 million bbl/day still transiting with military assistance. The July 18-19 expansion of Iranian strikes to Kuwait civilian infrastructure (desalination plant) is a qualitative step toward Saudi/UAE energy infrastructure risk and is reflected in the 0.38 baseline. Nine consecutive nights of US-Iran exchange have not triggered $100 — market has priced the current intensity.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if ICE Brent Crude front-month official settlement closes at or above $100.00/bbl on any single trading session between July 21 and Aug 3, 2026. Intraday touch without close at threshold = NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>ICE official settlement price. Bloomberg, Reuters, or CNBC commodity desk are acceptable TIER1 proxies.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If trading halt occurs on specific day, that day skipped; if next eligible day closes ≥$100, resolve YES. Exact $99.99 = NO. Contracts other than Brent front-month do not count.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IRGC attack confirmed on Saudi Aramco or ADNOC/UAE energy infrastructure</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Brent closes above $95 on any day before July 26</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran formally prohibits all Hormuz transits including military-escorted convoys</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30-90 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran and the US convene a formally structured negotiating session attended by minister or VP-level principals from both sides, publicly confirmed by both governments, covering at minimum two of: nuclear program, sanctions, Hormuz navigation, before EOD 2026-09-30?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">38%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −4pp from 42% (2026-07-20)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-30</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Analyst proposed p=0.42; Judge reduces to p=0.38. The Islamabad MoU 60-day window is de facto voided. FM Araghchi stated talks will not begin if threats continue. Diplomatic track is at its lowest point since Feb 28. Against: 72-day horizon is substantial; Iran's economic pressure provides structural incentive; Qatar and Pakistan maintained mediation investment; both sides went from hostilities to an MoU in 109 days (Feb 28 to June 17). F2 ceasefire is the gateway event. Judge reduction rationale: the Darkhovin nuclear plant strike (July 19) adds a new category of escalation — attacks on civilian nuclear infrastructure under IAEA safeguards — that is likely to impose more stringent Iranian preconditions for talks, compressing the already-tight timeline. The prior cycle started from Day 1 of war; this cycle starts from a worse diplomatic baseline than Day 1.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if a session occurs before EOD Sept 30: (a) attended by named US official at or above assistant secretary/deputy envoy level AND named Iranian official at or above deputy foreign minister level; (b) publicly confirmed by both governments' official spokespeople; (c) covering two or more of: nuclear program, sanctions, Hormuz management.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1 (Reuters, AP, AFP, Bloomberg) of both governments' official public acknowledgment. Iranian confirmation must come from a named official on record, not anonymous sourcing alone.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Proximity talks with mediators as sole intermediaries (no direct contact) count if publicly described as structured negotiations by both sides. If Iran confirms but US attributes to 'technical level only' = RESOLVE-NO. If both sides confirm but dispute topics, resolve YES if two covered topics appear in any credible account.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">New ceasefire (F2) confirmed before July 31</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran formally rescinds July 18 MoU suspension in named official statement</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Qatar FM and Pakistan FM both visit Tehran AND Washington within the same calendar week</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F6</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the 7-day rolling average of commercial vessel transits through the Strait of Hormuz reach 30 or more per day before EOD 2026-09-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">28%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">Δ −9pp from 37% (2026-07-20)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Analyst proposed p=0.37; Judge reduces to p=0.28. Current transit level ~10/day July 19-20, down from post-MoU peak ~43 July 3. Pre-war baseline 120-140/day; 30/day = ~21-25% of normal. June 17 MoU brought recovery from near-zero to ~43 in ~16 days; Iran's renewed attacks after July 7 reversed this within days. A second ceasefire (F2, p=0.18) is necessary but not sufficient; MCM operations must resume; major shippers require sustained confidence. Mechanical derivation: P(restored by Aug 10) ≤ 0.10; P(restored Aug 11-Sept 15 | not by Aug 10) ≈ 0.18 × 0.90 ≈ 0.162; total P ≈ 0.25. Judge sets 0.28 (EIA-reported 8.5 million bbl/day military-escorted throughput provides a floor for rapid commercial recovery if political conditions change). NOTE: EIA reports 8.5 million bbl/day via military escort versus ~10 AIS-tracked commercial transits — data conflict adds uncertainty; trend is toward continued closure.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if an authoritative shipping data source reports a 7-day rolling average of ≥30 confirmed commercial vessel transits through the Strait of Hormuz on any day before EOD Sept 15. Excludes warships and military support vessels but includes LNG, crude, and container ships with military escort.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>PortWatch (IMF), USNI News, Lloyd's List Intelligence, or MarineTraffic official data products. TIER1 news citing these sources with specific count data is acceptable.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If AIS data is systematically disrupted (transponders off for security) and counts are unreliable: hold resolution up to 7 days past horizon; if no clear data, resolve AMBIGUOUS. If 7-day average reaches 30 during a brief window before Iranian interdiction resumes, resolve YES if the 30 threshold was met on any single calculation date.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">New ceasefire (F2) confirmed before July 31</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM announces formal resumption of MCM operations post-July 7 Iranian interdiction</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">IMF PortWatch 7-day average exceeds 20/day for 3 consecutive calendar days</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 6-12 MONTHS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6-12 MONTHS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-domestic status-ACTIVE">
