  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>On July 18, an Iran-attributed drone struck US forces at Muwaffaq Salti Air Base in Jordan, killing three US Army soldiers and wounding five — the first confirmed US service-member fatalities in Operation Epic Fury. CENTCOM attributed the attack to the 'Islamic Resistance' umbrella under IRGC coordination; Iranian state media did not claim responsibility directly. The US conducted its ninth consecutive night of strikes on IRGC Khuzestan Province assets in response. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span>, <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>On July 18-19, Iranian ballistic missiles targeted Kuwait's Az-Zour desalination complex (five launches; two intercepted, three impacted the facility site), and aircraft approached the Al Udeid Air Base vicinity in Qatar. Kuwait's Ministry of Commerce and Industry confirmed structural damage to the Az-Zour facility. Qatar's Ministry of Foreign Affairs filed a formal diplomatic note to the Iranian Embassy in Doha — the first Iranian strike on a mediating state in the conflict — and the Qatari mediation channel confirmed no scheduled contact with Tehran as of July 20. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span>, <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>CENTCOM confirmed a July 19 strike on the Darkhovin Nuclear Power Plant construction site on the Karun River, Khuzestan Province — a civilian electricity facility under active IAEA safeguards. IAEA Director-General Grossi called for 'immediate restraint and strict prohibition of attacks on nuclear sites.' Iran MFA Spokesperson Baghaei stated Iran 'reserves the right to a proportional response' and described the strike as 'a new category of aggression.' No confirmed radioactive release. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>ICE Brent crude settled at $90.78 on July 19, a 6.9% gain from $84.95 on July 15. The Az-Zour desalination strike establishes a new category of Iranian targeting — Gulf state civilian economic infrastructure — that market participants read as expanding the potential target set toward Gulf energy facilities. The EIA reported 8.5 million barrels per day transiting via military escort as of July 12; Hormuz commercial AIS-tracked transits remained ~10/day. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>The 25th Knesset completed its final session July 17, with the dissolution bill passing 62-0 and all coalition partners voting for dissolution. Israel's Central Elections Committee confirmed October 27 as the date for elections to the 26th Knesset — the first full-term election in Israel since 1988. The Netanyahu government transitions to caretaker status; no coalition collapse or early election trigger occurred before the Oct 27 date. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

