      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path:</strong> A confirmed direct Iranian strike on Israeli territory (F1, p=0.28) or on Saudi/UAE energy infrastructure drives Brent above $100 (F3, p=0.38), triggering Israeli military response and drawing the conflict into a multi-front war exceeding the Feb-June 2026 exchange intensity.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> F2 ceasefire fails (p=0.82 NO), hostilities continue through the Sept 30 talks window, F6 Hormuz recovery stalls below 30/day (p=0.72 NO); the conflict settles into a managed-intensity phase of periodic strikes and blocked commercial shipping lasting through the Israeli election (F5, p=0.72).</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> F2 ceasefire holds before July 31 (p=0.18 YES), F4 talks resume by Sept 30 (p=0.38 YES), MCM operations restart and Hormuz commercial traffic recovers to F6 threshold (p=0.28 YES), and the October 27 Israeli election proceeds normally (F5, p=0.72).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>IRNA and Tasnim led coverage of the Jordan attack through the 'resistance martyrdom' framework — reporting that 'resistance forces carried out a dignified response to American aggression' without attributing direct IRGC responsibility. Kayhan's July 20 editorial described the Muwaffaq Salti attack as 'a proportionate response by the muqawama to the American presence in occupied Jordan.' IRGC-affiliated Tasnim News quoted IRGC Aerospace Commander Hajizadeh: 'We do not threaten; we act.' → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>State media converged on a single framing for the Darkhovin strike: 'terrorist attack on sacred civilian nuclear infrastructure.' All six monitored outlets ran identically-worded condemnations within 30 minutes of CENTCOM's announcement — a coordination pace associated with Supreme National Security Council directives. FM Araghchi's 'no talks if threats continue' statement was reprinted verbatim by IRNA, Tasnim, and Fars — a unified leadership posture indicating coordinated communication across the foreign-policy apparatus rather than an ad hoc remark. → supports <span class="cite">F4</span> without move</p>

      <p>On the domestic register, IRIB's nightly newscast July 19 foregrounded Iranian operational reach across Jordan, Kuwait, Qatar, and Syria — framing geographic expansion as demonstration of capability. The formal MoU suspension (Deputy FM Gharibabadi, July 18) received two paragraphs on IRNA versus eight paragraphs on the Darkhovin condemnation — a proportioning that downplays negotiation failure while amplifying grievance framing. Farsi-language social media monitoring by outside observers recorded civilian anxiety about the Darkhovin strike's safety implications, diverging from state-media confidence framing. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

